In C, you can terminate the execution of your program by using the `exit()` function from the `<stdlib.h>` library. This function takes an integer argument that represents the exit status of the program.

Here's an example:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");

    // Terminate the program with exit code 0 (success)
    exit(0);
}
```

In this example, after printing "Hello, World!", the program will call `exit(0)`, which terminates the program
